# Slow Ordered Collection: Identical to fast_unordered.intent PLUS ONE SENTENCE
# ("Keep items in the order they were added.")
# Causes remove-item to memmove AND free+calloc+rehash the entire hash table on EVERY delete!
Items is a collection.
Each item has a key (text), a code (number) and a val (number).
Keys are unique.
If an item already exists, replace it.
Keep items in the order they were added.

add-item: add an item.
find-item: find an item by key.
remove-item: remove an item by key.
count-items: how many items are there?
total-val: what is the total val of items?
